{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435560-seba-in-second-edition","id":1435560,"title":"Seba in second edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-15T08:47:35-08:00","id":1435560,"title":"Seba in second edition","content":"For the backers, are there rules about Seba in the 2e book? Or any conversion notes from 1e? I loved the Untouched and Broken seba.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T09:24:59-08:00","id":1435561,"title":"","content":"IIRC, there were no 2e conversion for Seba in the Core. The Book of Lasting Death, however, is supposed to give information about Minor Guilds, and the Deceived are such a Guild- so maybe we'll got a few in that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-16T05:48:10-08:00","id":1435632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435560-seba-in-second-edition#post1435560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the backers, are there rules about Seba in the 2e book? Or any conversion notes from 1e? I loved the Untouched and Broken seba.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in mechanical terms, though they are confirmed to be canon in the section on the Deceived - as LostLight said, they're considered a 'Minor Guild' this edition.<br /> <br /> That said, the idea of them may have been modified somewhat, as one of the 'They say X' bits about the Deceived mentions the idea of seba being Vessels <i>in potentia</i>, sort of the magical inspiration for another type of Vessel, stolen and made into a Vessel of another kind.<br /> <br /> And finally, regarding <i>Untouched and Broken</i> specifically, I've actually converted that one myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Untouched and Broken (\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Power</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">: The bearer\u2019s soul hardens against the magic and guile of others. The dice pool of any character attempting to outright lie to her, or target her with a supernatural power is reduced by 3, possibly to a chance die. If the 'attacker' knows the bearer's True Name this penalty is ignored. If the 'attacker' knows the bearer's more ordinary name, the penalty is reduced to 2. This does not apply against half-truths and subtler forms of manipulation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Curse</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Though hardened against those without, the bearer's wounded heart is numb to the pain of humanity. This chosen cruelty of Fate adds one to the target number of all rolls her player makes to resist Breaking Points. If their morality stat represents a balance between two extremes, such as a werewolf's Harmony, this penalty applies in a manner so as to encourage the being to become more inhuman. Beasts, those heartless monsters, instead experience a terrible expansion of their hunger, increasing their effective Satiety level by one (e.g. Low becomes Medium, Medium becomes High) for the purposes of determining the types of meal which will satisfy their soul's hunger.<br /> <br /> Mummies do not modify the target number of Memory Breaking Points, but instead subtract one die from their pools, to a minimum of 1. The Deceived ignore this curse entirely.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Seba are fucking awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-16-2021, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T02:43:42-08:00","id":1435832,"title":"","content":"Artistic Seba are basically relics in potentia due to being concepts that haven\u2019t crystallized into form, so it\u2019s accurate. That said, I\u2019m still convinced cosmic Seba are still lurking in the darkness beyond the world, waiting to rain down on us again during the next celestial convergence event besides the Sothic Turn...bringing us unknown treasures and untold horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T17:24:59-07:00","id":1495702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435560-seba-in-second-edition?p=1435561#post1435561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, there were no 2e conversion for Seba in the Core. The Book of Lasting Death, however, is supposed to give information about Minor Guilds, and the Deceived are such a Guild- so maybe we'll got a few in that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thread Necromancy but I dont want to make a new thread for the same topic.<br /> <br /> With the Book of Lasting Death, did we get Seba for 2e???<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T17:29:22-07:00","id":1495703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435560-seba-in-second-edition?p=1495702#post1495702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thread Necromancy but I dont want to make a new thread for the same topic.<br /> <br /> With the Book of Lasting Death, did we get Seba for 2e???</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mentioned, but we don't have a full write up on them-there's just no space for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not